# Moby-Dick oracle batch 3 (public domain, Melville d. 1891).
# Hand-tagged UPOS, UD tokenization (punctuation split, contractions
# split UD-style, ASCII apostrophes), EWT-side conventions per
# CANONICAL.md (predicative participles ADJ, reduced relatives VERB,
# temporal-when ADV, existentials There/PRON + VERB, subjunctive be
# AUX, lone all DET). Sentences from chapters 7-26 - disjoint from
# the ch.1-2 prose eval and the ch.4-6 oracle batches 01/02.
# Per-class-targeted: 3sg -s verbs, that/subordinator clauses,
# imperatives, titlecase PROPN, prep chains, participial ADJ/VERB.
# Contested calls (EWT train counts): that SCONJ/PRON/DET by
# construction (987/787/160); as+a ADP 106:1; as+PRON SCONJ 78:0;
# being AUX 139:5; No-one PRON 7:0; so-that SCONJ/SCONJ 26:0;
# as-though SCONJ/SCONJ 2:0; Much-subject ADJ 5:0 (EWT practice);
# other ADJ 268:1; several ADJ 49:0; such ADJ 72:24; bound ADJ 2:0;
# cleft-that: extraposition SCONJ (It-is-ADJ-that), PP-cleft PRON
# (out-of-X-that, cf first-time-that PRON/obl:unmarked); but before
# ADV kept CCONJ 87:0 (tension noted: "esteem but meanly").
